{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/95440-god-machine-chronicle-era-mantle-bonuses","id":95440,"title":"God-Machine Chronicle Era Mantle Bonuses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-21T00:38:51-07:00","id":95440,"title":"God-Machine Chronicle Era Mantle Bonuses","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I'm working on a conversion for <i>Changeling</i> to the God-Machine Chronicle ruleset, and while I was at it, I did a lot of tinkering with Courts and Mantles. The default Spring 3 bonus doesn't work anymore (half-price on certain merits), so like a good homebrewer, I ripped out the whole thing and rebuilt it from scratch.<br /> <br /> The design philosophy going in is to somewhat unify the Mantle mechanics (to help correct the 'Autumn Mantle is crap' problem). At the first dot, changelings get a Court Condition (borrowed from <i>Demon</i> because Agenda Conditions are cool)--the beat is gained from provoking problems with the court's emotion, the resolution gives a +3 bonus to something relevant to the court's concerns. At Mantle 3, the changeling gets (Mantle/2, round up) dots in a set array of Merits--not a huge bonus, especially for changelings, but flavorful. At Mantle 5, I figured the changeling would get an outright supernatural buff; I kinda cheated by just taking relevant mechanics from the previous Mantle rules.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring them to the community is partially to show off my work, and partially to get some feedback. I'm not confident on making Conditions yet, so insight on the Court Conditions would be appreciated; and if people have cooler ideas for the Mantle 3 and 5 bonuses, it'd be appreciated.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">SPRING</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">1: Condition: Spring Seduction (Gain a Beat when you convince someone to follow through with their desires when doing so is likely to detriment the character; Resolve the condition to gain +3 to a Social roll to tempt, convince, or bargain with a target.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">3: The character gains a number of dots split between Allies, Contacts, Fame, and Retainers equal to her half Mantle (round up).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">5: +1 to Socialize rolls, can reroll a Social roll meant to make a first impression once in a scene.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">SUMMER</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">1: Condition: Summer Battles (Gain a beat when you cause someone's wrath to go out of control, prompting a conflict\u2014physical, social, or mental; Resolve the condition to gain a +3 in a contested roll against a target that is angry at the changeling.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">3: The character gains a number of dots split between Fighting Styles equal to half her Mantle (round up)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">5: +4 dice to Strength from spending Willpower, +1 Health level</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">AUTUMN</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">1: Condition: Autumn Whispers (Gain a beat when you provoke extreme action using fear; Resolve the condition to gain a +3 to a roll meant to tell the changeling about an occult secret (this includes Contracts that heighten perceptions or give information).)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">3: The character gains a number of dots split between Harvest, Library, Pledgesmith, and Hedgebeast Companion equal to half her Mantle (round up).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">5: +1 to rolls that involve the True Fae, can reroll a failed Occult roll to understand or use magic (including Contracts) once in a scene.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\">WINTER</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">1: Condition: Winter Tears (Gain a beat when use a character's sorrow to dramatically change their current course of action; Resolve the condition to gain +3 to a roll meant to conceal the changeling or members of their motley.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">3: The character gains a number of dots split between Altered Identity, Anonymity, Fleet of Foot, and Hollow equal to half her Mantle (round up).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">5:+1 to Subterfuge rolls, characters are at a -3 to notice the changeling and their activities or movements.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T02:02:13-07:00","id":95468,"title":"","content":"Summer 5 is basically the Giant merit plus being an Ogre with Wyrd 5; compare that to your Spring 5. Hardly balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T03:23:32-07:00","id":95488,"title":"","content":"I'd use the mystery cult initiation rules as a guideline.<br /> <br /> I'd also remove the conditions you're using there. Each court has at least three important aspects: Their emotion, their methodology, their goal. I wouldn't prioritise their emotions this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:39:37-07:00","id":95671,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of what you are doing here. I am not super familiar with the God Machine Chronicle rules, however, so I am in no position to judge your rules-fu. That said ...<br /> <br /> I do like how the first tier of the Merits are all mechanical incentives to get players to act like weird fairies. Good stuff, I have always been fond of mechanics that encourage inventive roleplaying. The second tier boost to Merits seems a little boring. I mean, I get it. It makes sense. It's just that it seems a bit lackluster when compared to that first rad Mantle power. As for the last level, the idea is cool but unless the GMC mods completely changed the core mechanic of the game they seem pretty unbalanced in utility and power when compared with each other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T10:14:12-07:00","id":95737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/95440-god-machine-chronicle-era-mantle-bonuses?p=95468#post95468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summer 5 is basically the Giant merit plus being an Ogre with Wyrd 5; compare that to your Spring 5. Hardly balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both effects are just the default Mantle 1 and Mantle 5 bonuses stacked together (the +4 to Strength rolls from Willpower replaces the default +3). That said, yeah, Spring 5 is pretty lame. Perhaps gain the rote-action bonus to a single Socialize, Persuasion, Empathy, or Expression roll in a scene?<br /> <br /> At heart, my biggest problem in WoD stuff is that I'm godawful at making new cool powers, so if folks have better ideas for the kind of abilities Mantle 3 and 5 can grant, then by all means let me know. I'm keeping Court Conditions as a thing; I like those too much, though the specific wording can be freely tweaked.<br /> <br /> The Beat condition is meant to evoke the court's emotion in a way that corresponds to the court's core philosophy--catharsis through sorrow, wisdom through fear, strength from wrath, fulfillment through desire. I should probably switch back the Winter and Autumn trigger conditions; I have mental images of what those should look like (an Autumn courtier scaring an ignorant person away from a scary situation, a Winter courtier causing someone to break down into held-back tears from sorrow), but I'm not sure how to translate those into a mechanical thing.<br /> <br /> The resolution part of the Condition is meant to get directly at the court's shtick. Spring gets a bonus to socializing, Summer gets a bonus to competition, Autumn gets a bonus to knowing stuff, Winter gets a bonus to hiding. That part's pretty straightforward, and I don't think it puts too much emphasis on the court's emotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1812,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","user":"Deflare","date":". 03-21-2014, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T02:18:48-07:00","id":96250,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I hit the Mantle 5 abilities with a hammer to come up with actual distinctive abilities. They're potent, but they're also more interesting than they were before, and hopefully more even in utility<br /> <br /> Spring 5: Once per chapter, allies within sensory range of the changeling can automatically fulfill their Mask* as though they had severely risked their Mien, refreshing all spent Willpower.<br /> Summer 5: Once per chapter, the changeling can automatically win a Down and Dirty Combat.<br /> Autumn 5: Once per chapter, the changeling can use a single clause of any Contract that she knows about, even if she doesn't possess the Contract or its prerequisites; the changeling counts as having fulfilled the clause's catch.<br /> Winter 5: Once per chapter, the changeling can disappear from the world for a scene. Only characters who have an active pledge with the changeling can observe the character, or remember that she exists.<br /> <br /> *I'm borrowing Masques and Dirges from Vampire, renaming them Masks and Miens--the human self, and the fae self, with the full refresh being dependent on supporting one side to the detriment of the other.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T12:06:25-07:00","id":100820,"title":"","content":"...I'm also running GMC-ified Changeling. We just let Spring Court buy those Merits at 2 per 1 xp, and then we just applied the Autumn Mantle to a broader array of Contracts.<br /> That was it. It's been working great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:47:51-07:00","id":100995,"title":"","content":"I don't actually have any Spring PC players in my game at the moment, but I'd be going with the same vein as professional training (Get beats when you buy merits in that area).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}